															</div>
				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/cckinnison" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1185977); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=1185977&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1609254203" alt="CCKinnison" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=1185977)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/cckinnison" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1185977); return false;" >CCKinnison</a></span> <span class="odate time_1519099744 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">20 Feb 2018 04:09</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-3715981">
									

<p>I *know* every SCP stands on it's own, and cross-linking is not needed nor directly *desired*.</p>
<p>All that said&#8230; What if the source of the 2532-As is SCP-1000? It's dead straight up their alley. And we were given &quot;not forever&quot;.</p>
<p>But that requires thinking of the SCPs in an evolving world, which is not how they are written or meant to be taken. So just take it as an obscure possibility for someone to maybe stick into a Tale some day.</p>

							</div>

								
					
